29\\cdot \\frac{7}{29}=7.\n$$" 13194139535909 true] [17592186373969 1017 #edb/ref 17592186373970 13194139535909 true] [17592186373969 1089 "q-102320" 13194139535909 true] [17592186373969 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535909 true] [17592186373969 1100 "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535909 true] [17592186373969 1113 #uuid "1c635af5-ba45-5ad9-a96d-e17304471ae7" 13194139535909 true] [17592186373969 1145 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535909 true] [17592186373970 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373971 13194139535909 true] [17592186373970 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373972 13194139535909 true] [17592186373970 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373973 13194139535909 true] [17592186373970 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373974 13194139535909 true] [17592186373970 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373975 13194139535909 true] [17592186373970 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535909 true] [17592186373970 1041 "selection" 13194139535909 true] [17592186373970 1104 #edb/ref 17